#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build the H79 negative-result page from its machine-readable evidence."""
from __future__ import annotations
import html, json
from pathlib import Path
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]; D=R/'docs'
def e(x): return html.escape(str(x))
def main():
 c=json.loads((R/'evidence/h79_radhalo_run_card.json').read_text())
 h=c['holdout_dti']; u=c['correlation_overlap_vs_registry']; v=c['validator_output']
 body=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>H79 radiometric halo · GEMSDOE77</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/lia.css"></head><body><header><div class="wrap"><span class="brand">GEMSDOE77 · H79-RH</span><a href="index.html">Start here</a><a href="executive-summary.html">How to submit</a><a href="h79-radhalo.html" class="here">H79</a><a href="hypotheses.html">Hypotheses</a></div></header><main><div class="wrap">
<h1>H79: lagged radiometric alteration-halo pairing</h1>
<p class="verdict"><b>UNIQUE BYTES GENERATED; NEGATIVE RESULT. OK to download for inspection. NOT OK to submit.</b> Selector: not approved. The GeoTIFF passes every local format/range check, but {e(c['verdict_reason'])}</p>
<section class="card dl"><h2>Download the generated GeoTIFF</h2><a class="btn" download href="downloads/{e(Path(c['download_path']).name)}">Download .tif</a> <a class="btn alt" download href="downloads/{e(Path(c['download_path']).with_suffix('.zip').name)}">Download one-TIFF .zip</a>
<div class="chips"><span class="chip ok">Format: PASS</span><span class="chip bad">Holdout promotion: FAIL</span><span class="chip bad">Literal uniqueness: FAIL</span><span class="chip warn">Weekly slot used: NO</span></div>
<p><b>Name:</b> <code>{e(c['submission_name'])}</code><br><b>Note ({c['submission_note_chars']}/140):</b> <code>{e(c['submission_note'])}</code><br><b>SHA-256:</b> <code>{c['raster_sha256']}</code></p></section>
<h2>Scientific result</h2><p><b>Hypothesis:</b> {e(c['hypothesis'])}</p><p><b>Mechanism:</b> {e(c['mechanism'])}</p><p><b>Named mimic:</b> {e(c['named_non_fault_process_that_could_mimic_it'])}</p>
<table><tr><th>Evidence</th><th>Measured result</th></tr><tr><td>HOLDOUT-DTI</td><td>{h['score']:.5f} (95% CI {h['ci95'][0]:.5f}–{h['ci95'][1]:.5f}; <code>{h['evaluator_version']}</code>; {h['withheld_positive_pixels']:,} withheld positives)</td></tr><tr><td>Δ vs random</td><td>{h['delta_vs_random']['delta']:+.5f} (95% CI {h['delta_vs_random']['ci95'][0]:+.5f} to {h['delta_vs_random']['ci95'][1]:+.5f})</td></tr><tr><td>Current repository best</td><td>{h['current_repository_best']:.6f} HOLDOUT-DTI; H79 does not beat it</td></tr><tr><td>Leakage canary</td><td>max symmetric feature-only AUC {c['leakage_canary']['max_symmetric_auc']:.4f} ≤ 0.90: PASS</td></tr></table>
<h2>Uniqueness and the binding stop</h2><p>The pre-placement surface passed the requested rank gate: max |Spearman ρ| = {u['surface_max_abs_spearman']:.4f} ≤ 0.90. Final dots have max |ρ| = {u['final_dots_max_abs_spearman']:.4f}, but max forward overlap within 3 px is {u['final_dots_max_forward_overlap_3px']:.1f} &gt; 0.70, with {u['duplicate_firings']} firings. Protocol rule 1 therefore says stop. Only {u['registry_checked']} of {u['registry_expected']} rasters were readable/aligned; four malformed or grid-mismatched entries are separately logged. The decisive irregularity is stronger: a registry diagnostic is positive on all 5,167,373 footprint cells, so every non-empty candidate has 100% forward overlap. No private density exemption was applied.</p>
<h2>Format validation</h2><ul><li>Single band float32: {v['single_band_float32']}</li><li>Finite inside footprint / no NaN: {v['no_nan_inside_footprint']}</li><li>Values in [0,1]: {v['values_in_0_1']}</li><li>CRS, shape and transform match: {v['crs_shape_transform_match']}</li><li>Positive mapped-catalogue cells: 0; binary dots: {v['dot_count']:,}</li></ul>
<h2>Candidate register and sources</h2><p><a href="research/h79_radhalo_hypotheses.md">Five preregistered geological hypotheses</a> name layers, signatures, off-catalogue rationale, differences and mimics. H79 implemented only rank 1. Official manual-review links: <a href="https://www.usgs.gov/data/geodawn-airborne-magnetic-and-radiometric-surveys-northwestern-great-basin-nevada-and">USGS GeoDAWN release</a>; <a href="https://www.drivendata.org/competitions/306/competition-doe-gems/page/967/">official problem description</a>; <a href="https://github.com/drivendataorg/gems-prize-reference-solution">official reference solution</a>.</p>
<h2>Why the reported H33 0.2778 remains stronger</h2><p>The repository's prior forensic analysis attributes H33's owner-reported result to sparse 300 m-spaced dots on an empirically enriched H19-5 structural support, plus removal near mapped faults. H79 instead tests an orthogonal radiometric mechanism. Its HOLDOUT-DTI is statistically indistinguishable from random and far below the current local best, so there is no evidence it will exceed 0.2778 or the 0.4413 public-leader value recorded in this repository. No organizer score is claimed for H79.</p>
<p><a href="downloads/h79_radhalo_run_card.json">Machine-readable run card</a> · <a href="evidence/h79_radhalo_e2_holdout.json">holdout evidence</a> · <a href="evidence/h79_radhalo_e3_uniqueness.json">uniqueness evidence</a></p>
</div></main></body></html>'''
 (D/'h79-radhalo.html').write_text(body)
if __name__=='__main__': main()
